# Archetype Orchestrator: Cursor Rules

> These rules are enforced by git hooks. Skipping steps will block commits.

## Session Start: Required
1. **MANDATORY: Search open-brain at the START of EVERY task. No exceptions.** Do this BEFORE your first action. Run two searches: one for the task topic, one for "user preferences formatting rules". This applies to every task: coding, debugging, docs, research, refactoring, reviews, questions. Every task. Period.
2. Read `docs/planning/CONTEXT_CHECKPOINTS.md` if it exists
3. Run pre-work gate: `bash archetype-orchestrator/scripts/pre-work-check.sh`

## Branch Rules
- **Never commit to `main`, `master`, or `develop`**. The hook will block it
- Always use a feature branch: `git checkout -b feat/description`

## Discover Before Coding
- Scan: `python archetype-orchestrator/engine/discover.py --scan`
- Route: `python archetype-orchestrator/engine/discover.py --query "keywords"`
- Read the matched constitution before writing any code

## During Work
- Checkpoint at milestones: `bash archetype-orchestrator/scripts/context-checkpoint.sh "milestone"`
- If open-brain MCP is available, call `capture_context` with decisions and gotchas, passing `source="cursor"`

## Destructive Operations
- Never run `rm -rf`, `git reset --hard`, or force-push without explicit user confirmation
- State exactly what will be affected and wait for approval

## Post-Work Gate
```bash
bash archetype-orchestrator/scripts/post-work-check.sh
```
For release-impacting changes: update `CHANGELOG.md` and bump version.

## Validation
```bash
bash archetype-orchestrator/scripts/validate.sh
```
Must pass before committing. Checks: secrets, code safety, semver, conventional commits.

## Planning Documents (docs/planning/)
- DUAL_AGENT_WORKFLOW.md
- CONTEXT_LOOP.md
